  "correct_answer": "1633",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#8230;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now finding the sum of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>101</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>&nbsp;Prime factors of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;Multiples of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mi>B</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;Multiples of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;Multiples of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>So&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8746;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mi>B</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>To have H.C.F to be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;we need to subtract the sum of multiples of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;from&nbsp;sum of set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>&nbsp;to get required answer,</p><p>So required answer</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>101</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8722;</mo></math>&nbsp;Sum of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8746;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>101</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>51</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>33</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mn>102</mn></mfenced><mo>&#8722;</mo><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>102</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1633</mn></math></p>"
